  "slug": "daring-club-motema-pembe",
  "summary": "Daring Club Motema Pembe (DCMP) is a Kinshasa football club founded in 1936 by missionary Father Raphaël de la Kethulle. Originally called Daring de Bruxelles, it became CS Imana in 1949 and adopted its current name in 1985.\n\nDCMP has won 27 national titles since 1963, making it the Democratic Republic of the Congo’s most successful club by domestic honours. Its successes include 12 league titles and a record 14 Congo Cups. In 1994, it won the African Cup Winners’ Cup, its major continental title.\n\nThe club endured internal conflict and declining support during the 2010s, including a 2014 split that led to the formation of a separate CS Imana.",
